## Summary
Errors in message handlers are logged but handlers keep being invoked forever. Should disable after threshold failures.

## Location
`memberships/src/main/java/com/hellblazer/delos/membership/messaging/rbc/ReliableBroadcaster.java:213-219`

## Current Code (NO CIRCUIT BREAKER)
```java
handlers.forEach(handler -> {
    try {
        handler.accept(content);
    } catch (Throwable e) {
        log.error("Error in handler", e);
        // Handler still invoked next time!
    }
});
```

## Fix
Track consecutive failures per handler, disable after threshold:
```java
private final Map<Consumer<?>, AtomicInteger> handlerFailures = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
private static final int CIRCUIT_BREAKER_THRESHOLD = 10;

handlers.forEach(handler -> {
    if (handlerFailures.getOrDefault(handler, new AtomicInteger()).get() >= CIRCUIT_BREAKER_THRESHOLD) {
        return; // Circuit open
    }
    try {
        handler.accept(content);
        handlerFailures.remove(handler); // Reset on success
    } catch (Throwable e) {
        log.error("Error in handler", e);
        handlerFailures.computeIfAbsent(handler, k -> new AtomicInteger()).incrementAndGet();
    }
});
```

Add reset mechanism after backoff period or explicit reset API.

## Impact
- Failing handlers waste CPU
- Error log spam
- Potential cascading failures

## Verification
- Add test for circuit breaker behavior
- Verify reset after backoff

