## Summary
Successors are contacted sequentially with sleep delay between each. Total round time = successors.size() × (gossip_latency + duration). Should parallelize for O(duration + max(latency)).

## Location
`memberships/src/main/java/com/hellblazer/delos/membership/messaging/rbc/ReliableBroadcaster.java:281-293`

## Current Code (SEQUENTIAL)
```java
successors.forEach(i -> {
    var link = comm.connect(i.m());
    if (link != null) {
        var g = gossipRound(link, i.ring());
        if (g != null) handle(g, link, i.ring(), startNanos);
    }
    Thread.sleep(duration.toMillis());  // Sleep after EACH successor
});
```

Example: 6 successors, 10ms duration, 5ms gossip latency → 90ms per round

## Fix
Parallel fan-out with single delay:
```java
List<CompletableFuture<Reconcile>> futures = successors.stream()
    .map(i -> CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {
        var link = comm.connect(i.m());
        return link != null ? gossipRound(link, i.ring()) : null;
    }, executor))
    .toList();

CompletableFuture.allOf(futures.toArray(new CompletableFuture[0])).join();
futures.stream()
    .map(CompletableFuture::join)
    .filter(Objects::nonNull)
    .forEach(g -> handle(g, ...));

Thread.sleep(duration.toMillis());  // Single delay after all
```

## Impact
- Current: O(n × duration) round latency
- Fixed: O(duration + max(gossip_latency)) round latency
- With maxAge=6, messages get ~6× more propagation opportunities

## Verification
- Add latency benchmark comparing sequential vs parallel
- Measure message propagation time across cluster

