Create a single KerlValidator service to centralize KERL validation logic currently duplicated across Gorgoneion, Thoth, and witness service.

## Current State
- Gorgoneion.validateChain() - KERL chain validation
- Thoth Ani.kerlValidate() - KERL set validation
- Stereotomy KeyEventProcessor - Event processing
- Multiple places call similar validation logic

## Proposed Design
```java
public class KerlValidator {
    private final KERL kerl;
    private final EventValidation validation;

    // Core validation methods
    ValidationResult validate(KERL_ kerl);
    ValidationResult validateChain(List<KeyEvent> events);
    ValidationResult validateInception(InceptionEvent event);
    ValidationResult validateRotation(RotationEvent event, KeyState priorState);

    // Security checks
    boolean checkSignatureChain(List<KeyEvent> events);
    boolean checkSequenceIntegrity(List<KeyEvent> events);
    boolean checkDigestChain(List<KeyEvent> events);
    boolean checkWitnessThreshold(KeyEvent event, List<Receipt> receipts);
}
```

## Benefits
- Single source of truth for KERL validation
- Consistent security checks across all components
- Easier to audit and harden
- Reduced code duplication

## Affected Modules
