## Summary
tick() is only called after successful gossip in handle(). When gossipRound() fails, handle() is never called, tick() never executes - round counter stalls while wall-clock time advances.

## Location
`memberships/src/main/java/com/hellblazer/delos/membership/messaging/rbc/ReliableBroadcaster.java:258`

## Current Code (SKIPS ON FAILURE)
```java
private void handle(Reconcile gossip, ...) {
    try {
        buffer.receive(gossip.getUpdatesList());
        // ... reconciliation ...
    } finally {
        buffer.tick();  // Only if handle() called
    }
}

// But gossipRound() can return null (lines 231-238), skipping handle()
```

## Fix
Decouple tick() from gossip success:
```java
private void oneRound(...) {
    try {
        // ... gossip to successors ...
    } finally {
        buffer.tick();  // Always advance round
        notifyRoundListeners();
        schedule(duration, scheduler);
    }
}
```

## Impact
- Round-based metrics become meaningless
- Age-based eviction timing breaks (messages persist longer)
- Coordinated protocol actions drift out of sync

## Verification
- Add test for round counter under gossip failures
- Validate tick() called regardless of network state

