Fix approach:
Add trace/debug logging (not fail-fast, as connection-closed exceptions are expected in some scenarios):

```java
} catch (JdbcSQLNonTransientException | JdbcSQLNonTransientConnectionException e) {
    log.trace("Event operation failed (connection likely closed): {}", e.getMessage());
}
```

Complexity: 1-2 hours
Risk: LOW - Logging only, no behavior change

Testing: Verify log output in scenarios where connection is closed

Note: Not making this fail-fast per substantive-critic analysis - non-transient connection exceptions indicate connection is dead, nothing to do.

