## Summary
Parameters.Builder accepts invalid values without validation. No checks for sensible ranges or relationships between parameters.

## Location
`memberships/src/main/java/com/hellblazer/delos/membership/messaging/rbc/ReliableBroadcaster.java` - Parameters class

## Current State
No validation - accepts:
- bufferSize=0
- FPR > 1
- maxMessages > bufferSize
- Negative values

## Fix
Add validation in build():
```java
public Parameters build() {
    if (bufferSize <= 0) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("bufferSize must be positive: " + bufferSize);
    }
    if (maxMessages <= 0 || maxMessages > bufferSize) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("maxMessages must be in (0, bufferSize]: " + maxMessages);
    }
    if (falsePositiveRate <= 0 || falsePositiveRate >= 1) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("falsePositiveRate must be in (0, 1): " + falsePositiveRate);
    }
    if (maxMessageSize <= 0) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("maxMessageSize must be positive: " + maxMessageSize);
    }
    return new Parameters(bufferSize, maxMessages, falsePositiveRate, maxMessageSize, ...);
}
```

## Impact
- Invalid configurations fail silently or cause subtle bugs
- Harder to diagnose misconfiguration

## Verification
- Add tests for validation
- Test boundary conditions

